    "notes": {
      "dead_loop": "`send` iterates `recipients` and `return`s inside the loop, so only the first iteration ever runs: the message is addressed to `recipients[0]` and delivered to all of them. The `throw` after the loop is reachable only for an empty list.",
      "clock": "`send` calls `createExchangeMessage` with five arguments, so `datetime` and `dig` are `undefined` and `exchange(...)` falls back to `nowUTC()` — the message's `dt`, and therefore its SAID and every signature over it, depend on when it was built",
      "two_identifiers": "`send(name, topic, sender, ...)` takes the alias that addresses the resource and the identifier whose keeper signs as two independent arguments; nothing compares them",
      "return_types": "`sendFromEvents` declares `Promise<Exn>` while the sibling `Ipex.submit*` methods declare `Promise<ExchangeOperation>` for the same shape of POST to the same agent. Both are `res.json()` casts, so at most one can be right and neither is checked.",
      "routes": "the thirteen exported route constants are Roadmap 8.1's, not this item's: they are recorded here to pin the split, and because `send`'s route argument is the plain `string` they are values of"
    }
  },
